WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.960
He is the most bankable star in Hollywood
– an action hero with a massive, ripped

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.730
physique who has impeccable comedic timing
and a never ending supply of charm.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:14.119
He is also one of the greatest wrestling superstars
to ever emerge from the stables of the WWE

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:18.170
and the only third generation wrestling star
in history.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:24.099
The story of Dwayne Johnson – the Rock – is
a tale of dedication, grit and old fashioned

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:25.099
hard work.

00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:31.560
In this week’s Biographics we chart the
rise and rise of 2016’s Sexiest Man Alive

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:37.850
– Dwayne Johnson.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:51.770
Formative Years
Dwayne Douglas Johnson was born on May 2nd,

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.730
1972 in Hayward County, California.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:59.690
His mother Ata was of Samoan origin, while
his father, Wayde, was a Black Nova Scotian.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:04.470
Wayde earned his living as a professional
wrestler under the name of ‘Rocky Johnson’.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.470
To further entrench the wrestling gene in
his blood, Dwayne’s material grandfather

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:11.930
had also been a professional wrestler.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:16.940
Promoted as High Chief Peter Maivia, he was
the first Samoan wrestler to break into the

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:17.940
big time.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.560
A generation later, Rocky became the first
black champion to conquer the state wrestling

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.560
scene.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.410
Rocky hustled as a wrestler, taking on bouts
wherever he could in order to support his

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:28.410
family.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:32.170
Times were tough with the family moving from
state to state to keep pace with the wrestling

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.170
venues.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:37.550
In fact, during Dwayne’s formative years,
the family of three lived in 38 of the 50

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:41.340
states as they became entrenched in the gypsy
wrestling lifestyle.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.530
The only time Dwayne got to see his dad was
when he went on the road with him.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.659
He cherished these times and quickly fell
in love with everything to do with professional

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:50.659
wrestling.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:53.670
His dad taught him some basic moves, including
the sleeper hold.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.460
When he was eleven, Dwayne was ‘playing’
wrestling one school lunchtime when he put

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.440
the sleeper hold on a schoolmate.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.700
The kid immediately passed out.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.570
Unfortunately, Rocky hadn’t shown his son
how to bring someone out of the sleeper hold.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:08.410
The ambulance and the police were called and
Rocky had to come down to revive the student.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:12.299
The Johnson house became a hangout for Dwayne’s
school-mates, who knew that they were going

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:14.989
to have to go several rounds with their host.

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:18.849
Dwayne would turn these events into mock TV
shows, where he would pretend to interview

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:19.849
the wrestlers.

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:22.310
He would even interview himself as he portrayed
the bad guy.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:27.489
His showmanship was immediately evident as
he came out with all sorts of outrageous pronouncements

00:02:27.489 --> 00:02:29.549
against his intended victims.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.629
Dwayne excelled in a number of sports.

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:33.239
Physically he was miles ahead of his classmates.

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:37.329
He had his first weights workout when he was
thirteen, but he’d been tagging along with

00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:39.639
his dad to the gym since he was 5 years old.

00:02:39.639 --> 00:02:45.170
As he sat quietly on a bench and watched proudly
as Rocky pounded out set after set with gargantuan

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:49.879
weights, Dwayne breathed in the gym atmosphere
and marvelled at the sight of huge men doing

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:53.610
seemingly impossible things with massive loads
of iron.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:58.079
While other dads took their kids to the playground,
Rocky took Dwayne to some of the most hardcore

00:02:58.079 --> 00:02:59.500
gyms in the country.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.710
It was here that the future superstar learned
that there was no replacement for pure, gut

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.219
wrenching hard work.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:18.129
A Love Affair with Iron is Born
At the age of eight, Rocky allowed Dwayne

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:19.760
to participate in sports.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.090
He tried baseball, soccer, martial arts and
gymnastics.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:25.030
What he was really longing to do was to start
lifting weights, but he’d have to wait a

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.310
few more years for that.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:32.409
Finally, on his 13th birthday, his dad took
him to a local gym for his first ever weights

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:33.409
workout.

00:03:33.409 --> 00:03:37.480
An obvious place to start was the bench press,
which he’d studied for years as his dad

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.659
and others pressed massive amounts of steel
from their chest.

00:03:40.659 --> 00:03:43.500
Rocky had his son start with an unloaded bar.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:48.879
He pumped out 10 reps with no problem, so
Rocky added a 20-pound plate to each end.

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:51.799
This time Dwayne pushed out 8 easy reps.

00:03:51.799 --> 00:03:55.439
Impressed, Rocky asked his son if he wanted
to try the 45 pounders.

00:03:55.439 --> 00:03:56.819
Dwayne nodded his head.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:04:01.230
His dad stood behind him and lifted the bar
off the supports – and Dwayne got buried

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.489
under the 135-pound weight.

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:07.199
He felt embarrassed and ashamed – as if
he had let his dad down.

00:04:07.199 --> 00:04:10.489
That feeling fuelled an intense desire to
get better at the bench press and within a

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:14.089
few years he would be bench pressing 400 pounds.

00:04:14.089 --> 00:04:17.530
Between the ages of 14 and 15, Dwayne excelled
in the gym.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.819
By the time he entered high school he had
grown to a towering 6 foot 3 inches and tipped

00:04:21.819 --> 00:04:24.780
the scales at 225 pounds.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.639
His imposing physicality gave him a great
deal of self-confidence, which sometimes bordered

00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:30.639
on arrogance.

00:04:30.639 --> 00:04:31.639
Eve though he had developed a healthy dose
of self-discipline in the gym, his unstable

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:35.870
home life, that saw his father constantly
travelling, left him directionless when he

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.520
wasn’t pounding the weights.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.080
As a result, he started getting into trouble.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.780
It came to a head when he was fifteen and
got arrested for check fraud.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.240
His parents had to come to collect him from
the place station.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.260
When he looked at his mother and father he
realized that, despite living from paycheck

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.770
to paycheck, he was the biggest source of
stress in their lives.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:58.120
In that moment he vowed that he would never
cause problems for his folks again.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.449
Although that was the last time Dwayne got
arrested, it wasn’t the last time he caused

00:05:01.449 --> 00:05:03.220
worry for Rocky and Ata.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:07.039
In fact, the very next day at school he got
into a fight and knocked the other kid out.

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.110
It earned him a two-week suspension.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.861
Upon returning to school he decided that the
student’s bathroom was not good enough for

00:05:12.861 --> 00:05:15.140
him and so he decided to use the teacher’s
one.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:19.229
When asked to leave he was rude to the teacher
and tried to intimidate him with his physical

00:05:19.229 --> 00:05:20.229
presence.

00:05:20.229 --> 00:05:22.950
That night Dwayne felt pangs of guilt at the
way he had treated the teacher.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:27.189
So, the next day, he marched into the teacher’s
class and holding out his hand, said that

00:05:27.189 --> 00:05:30.280
he wanted to apologise for the way he had
acted the day before.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.480
The teacher stared at Dwayne’s hand for
a moment then grabbed it and told Dwayne that

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.849
he appreciated the apology.

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:37.889
Then, still holding the boy’s hand, he said.

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:50.500
“I want you to play football for me.”

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.500
Football Star

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.750
Football proved to be a positive outlet for
Dwayne’s frustrations and aggressions, providing

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.750
him with a renewed sense of focus.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:01.650
Under the watchful eye of coach Jody Cwick,
he steadily improved, both as a student and

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:02.650
as an athlete.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.719
By the time he was a high school senior he
was ranked as one of the top 10 defensive

00:06:06.719 --> 00:06:12.099
tackles in the country and was offered a scholarship
to the University of Miami, the No.1 college

00:06:12.099 --> 00:06:13.700
team in the United States.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:18.229
At Miami, Dwayne’s combination of size,
strength and athleticism coupled with his

00:06:18.229 --> 00:06:21.310
strong work ethic made him a standout from
the very beginning.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.780
Practices were going great and he was primed
to be the only freshman to play on the Varsity

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:26.780
team.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.110
But then tragedy struck.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:31.669
On the last day of practice with pads, he
crashed to the ground under the full weight

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:32.669
of his shoulder.

00:06:32.669 --> 00:06:35.419
It was dislocated and a number of ligaments
were torn.

00:06:35.419 --> 00:06:40.199
That night he had reconstruction surgery and
was told that he’d need a year to recover.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:43.510
He was put before the season had even begun.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:47.219
Dwayne fell into a deep depression, not even
bothering to go to class.

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:52.190
Then, without even attempting any of his mid-terms,
he hopped on a flight and returned home, which

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:54.069
at that time was in Tampa, Florida.

00:06:54.069 --> 00:06:57.550
After a couple of weeks he got a call from
Miami’s head coach, Dennis Erickson.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.410
He told Dwayne that he wanted him back at
school in two days.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:01.960
He wanted to talk to him.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.129
When they met up, Erickson was furious with
Johnson.

00:07:04.129 --> 00:07:07.080
He told him that he had embarrassed himself
and the team.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.590
Erickson had trusted him with a position of
responsibility and leadership and he had completely

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:12.590
let him down.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:15.510
Erickson then placed Dwayne under academic
probation.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:20.840
He was to attend every class, every practice
and every game – sitting on the sideline.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.669
However, to get into daily practice he had
to get the signatures of every one of his

00:07:24.669 --> 00:07:27.910
professors attesting that he had been to class
that day.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.280
If he didn’t, he would lose his scholarship.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.409
Dwayne dug deep and did what had to be done.

00:07:33.409 --> 00:07:37.870
He eventually became academic captain and
in his junior year was pre-season All-American.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:42.659
He graduated from Miami University in 1995
with a Bachelor of General Studies in criminology

00:07:42.659 --> 00:07:43.659
and physiology.

00:07:43.659 --> 00:07:48.270
It was at the University of Miami that Dwayne
met Dany Garcia, his future wife.

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:52.340
They were married in 1997 and divorced 10
years later.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:56.759
After a year’s injury recovery, Dwayne wasn’t
quite a fast or as mobile on the football

00:07:56.759 --> 00:07:57.759
field.

00:07:57.759 --> 00:07:59.770
He was circuit from the team and replaced
by Warren Sapp.

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:04.319
After graduation from Miami Dwayne went to
Calgary, Canada as a practice squad player

00:08:04.319 --> 00:08:05.900
for the Stampeders.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.370
Things were tough for him in Canada.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.689
He had hardly any money and few prospects.

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:15.860
But things got worse when he was cut from
the Stampeders squad after just two months.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:26.490
A Wrestler Like His Dad
Arriving back at his parents’ tiny apartment

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:29.509
in Tampa, Dwayne was now at rock bottom.

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:31.550
His football career was effectively over.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:33.520
He needed to look in another direction.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:39.060
He dug deep and realized that all of his life
his passion had been professional wrestling.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.660
If he never turned his hand to it, he would
forever be unfulfilled.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:46.530
And if he was going to step into that world,
now was the time.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:51.890
His mother and girlfriend encouraged him to
go for it, but Dwayne’s dad had major reservations.

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:56.260
Rocky knew firsthand just how tough the life
of a wrestler was and he wanted more for his

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.260
son.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:02.730
Yet, he vowed to stand behind his son, so
long as he put 11% effort into becoming successful.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.480
Rocky now became Dwayne’s full-time wrestling
coach.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.550
From the start, though, he taught him much
more than wrestling moves.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.720
He taught him how to be a showman.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:14.620
After a few months of intensive work, Rocky
felt his son was ready to take the next step.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:18.900
He got in touch with a former wrestler named
Pat Patterson who was now a talent agent.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:22.450
Patterson came to check out what Dwayne looked
like in the ring.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:25.080
Impressed he arranged for a signing with the
WWE.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:29.470
Dwayne was put into the minor leagues and
was given the name ‘Rocky Maivia’ in homage

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:31.850
to both his father and grandfather.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:36.080
He started wrestling in small arenas for $20
a pop, but it didn’t take long before he

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.080
got his break.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:42.890
The 1996 WWE Survivor series was televised
live on TV from Madison Square Garden – and

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.540
the new kid on the block was ‘Rocky Maivia.’

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.700
He made an immediate impression, establishing
himself as a rising WWE star by becoming the

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.140
last man standing.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:57.290
Rocky Maivia took on a charismatic, in your
face persona which proved to be too loud and

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:00.190
arrogant for many diehard WWE fans.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:05.570
His character was rejected for being too tacky
and fans came to see Rocky Maivia as an extremely

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:06.940
unlikeable character.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:11.430
When he wrestled the stadium would be littered
with signs reading ‘Rocky Sucks’ and ‘Die

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.430
Rocky, Die.’

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:17.520
But his perseverance and the constant refining
of his character eventually won the fans over.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:21.980
Fans came to appreciate that Rocky’s narcissism
was tongue in cheek, much in the mould of

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:25.690
Muhammad Ali and they began to enjoy his over
the top sense of humour.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:29.270
When he shortened his name to ‘The Rock’,
the fans embraced it and, within a year, he

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:43.970
had transformed the wrestler everyone loved
to hate to the ‘people’s champ.’

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.330
Dominating the WWE
Throughout 1997 and 1998 the Rock had ongoing

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:50.560
battles with Stone Cold Steve Austin, Triple
H and Mankind.

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:55.200
Throughout 1999 the WWF championship belt
passed between The Rock and Mankind several

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.780
times during a series of epic encounters.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:02.610
Then towards the end of ‘99, the two teamed
up to become the Rock ‘n Sock Connection

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:05.920
and going on to win the tag team championship
three times.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:09.870
The Rock and Mankind also performed comedy
skits on WWE live telecasts.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:14.500
One of them was a take-off of This is Your
Life in which Mankind interviewed people from

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.530
the Rock’s past.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:20.040
The segment drew an 8.4 Nielsen rating, one
of the highest ever for a WWE segment.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:25.260
In 2001, the Rock was suspended indefinitely
during the airing of Raw is War.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.680
He used the suspension as an opportunity to
move into the acting arena.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.680
Still, he would return again and again to
the wrestling ring.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:34.170
In 2011 he was the host of Wrestlemania 2011.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:39.400
He spent a large part of the promo build up
insulting and taunting John Cena, who he had

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.300
already been calling out on social media.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.710
A feud developed between the two which continued
for another two years.

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:49.530
When he finally stepped away from the wrestling
ring in 2016 The Rock had established himself

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:52.200
as one of the great pro wrestlers of all time.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:57.120
Hulk Hogan, himself a dominating WWE figure,
referred to him as ‘the biggest superstar

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.420
in the business’, a sentiment which was
echoed by John Cena.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:04.760
One of his many catch-phrases, ‘lay the
smackdown’, inspired the title of television’s

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.480
second longest running TV series, Smackdown!

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:10.390
The Rock has also entrenched himself in the
WWE record books.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:15.260
He was the first wrestler to win the WWF / WWE
championship seven times.

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:20.141
And his intercontinental championship reign
of 265 days is the longest in the modern era.

00:12:20.141 --> 00:12:33.850
A New Career Beckons
Dwayne’s huge popularity as a WWE character

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.730
allowed him to cross over into mainstream
media.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:41.830
His first acting job was in a 1999 episode
of That 70’s Show in which played his own

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:42.830
father.

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:45.780
In 2000, he appeared in Star Trek: Voyager
as an alien wrestler.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:49.740
His first movie appearance was a small role
in 2001’s The Mummy Returns.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:55.370
The movie was a smash hit, leading to a reprisal
of his role, this time as the lead, in The

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.570
Scorpion King.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:13:00.980
Johnson was paid $5.5 million for the role,
earning him a spot in the Guinness Book of

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:06.510
Records as the highest paid actor in a debut,
despite it actually being his second movie.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:09.040
The Scorpion King established Johnson as a
bona fide star.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.830
With his comedic talents clearly established
through his wrestling career, his next film,

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:15.880
the action comedy The Rundown was a natural
next step.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.680
This was followed up with a remake of the
true story of kick-ass sheriff Buford Pusser

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:18.680
in Walking Tall.

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:23.220
This role cemented Johnson’s position as
the ultimate hard as nails action hero with

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.220
a heart of gold.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:28.840
Over the next few years, Dwayne skipped between
comedies and action movies with such films

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:33.070
as Be Cool, Doom, Tooth Fairy (a film which
was originally written for one of the Rock’s

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:36.390
heroes, Arnold Schwarzenegger) and The Fast
and The Furious franchise.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:40.950
His debut in Fast and Furious came in the
fifth movie, after fans demanded to see a

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:43.450
showdown between Johnson and Vin Diesel.

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:49.290
The movie was the most successful in the entire
franchise, making more than $86 million on

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:50.670
its opening weekend.

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:54.230
This remains the biggest opening for any Johnson
movie.

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:58.200
Dwayne has interspersed his movie roles with
appearances on a number of TV shows, many

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.010
of them aimed at a pre-teen audience.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:05.220
He appeared in episodes of Cory in the House
and The Wizards of Waverly Place and was the

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:08.620
host of the Nickelodeon Kid’s Choice Awards
in 2009.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:12.900
That year he also appeared several times on
Saturday Night Live where he introduced his

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:22.390
Rock Obama character, a morphing of President
Obama with the Incredible Hulk.

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:29.880
Superstar
By the end of the 2000’s, Johnson had developed

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:35.050
a reputation as a bankable star who could
not only carry a new movie, but also had a

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:38.520
proven record of being able to revive franchises
that were getting tired.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:42.380
He became known as a very busy actor, with
at least a couple of new movies coming out

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.000
each year.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.930
In 2013, Johnson starred in a couple of true
life-based movie, Pain and Gain and Empire

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:48.930
State.

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:52.820
He also announced that year that he was to
executive produce and star in an HBO TV series

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:57.060
set in the world of professional football
called Ballers.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:15:01.310
In December, 2013, Forbes magazine named Johnson
as the highest paid actor of the year, with

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:03.870
earnings of $1.3 billion.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:09.200
Ballers, which debuted on HBO in June 2015,
proved to be a huge success.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:13.700
Johnson, who plays Spencer Strathmore, a retired
NFL player who has gone on to a career as

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:18.310
a financial planner for current NFL players,
received props for his charm and depth.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.340
As of 2018, the show is into its fourth season.

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:24.670
In 2014, Johnson played the title character
in Hercules.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:28.920
For this role he stepped up his already gruelling
workout and nutrition protocol in order to

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.440
get as impressively muscular as possible.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:35.410
He followed this up with the huge disaster
hit San Andreas, before switching back to

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.830
comedy with Central Intelligence, alongside
Kevin Hart.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:43.730
2016 saw Johnson teaming with Zac Efron for
a feature movie version of the classic beach

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.810
and babes TV series Baywatch.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:50.510
The two hulky actors created a lot of pre-release
buzz with their epic beach workouts in which

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:54.300
Johnson would present Efron with gut-busting
physical challenges.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.910
The movie, however, was a box office disappointment.

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:01.470
Johnson finished out 2016 by learning that
he had been voted People Magazine’s Sexiest

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:02.470
Man Alive.

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:06.490
The next big project was a remake of the Robin
Williams classic Jumanji.

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:11.060
Johnson, along with co-stars Jack Black and
Kevin Hart, brought a new, updated angle to

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:13.410
the story that resonated with fans.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:17.900
The movie has so far brought in $829 million
on a $90 million budget.

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:31.020
The Rock’s Anchor
Throughout his life Dwayne has had one constant

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:36.200
that has kept him grounded and which he credits
as the basis of everything that he has achieved;

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.200
the gym.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:40.640
From those earliest days when he would sit
and watch his father dominate the weights

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:45.920
in the 1970’s, the sights, smells and sounds
of working out became an integral part of

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:46.920
his being.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:50.550
Dwayne’s workout intensity and dedication
have been an inspiration to millions.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:55.540
He hits the gym at 4 o’clock every morning,
training for up to 2 hours with heavy basic

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:59.950
compound moves, interspersed with cardio to
keep his body fat percentage into the single

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:00.950
digits.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:05.300
He is a favourite with the bodybuilding community,
appearing as a guest host at the 2016 Mr.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:06.589
Olympia competition.

00:17:06.589 --> 00:17:10.480
Since 2014, Dwayne has been living in Southwest
Ranches in Florida.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:15.210
His first child, Simone, was born in 2001,
while he was still married to her mother,

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.210
Dany.

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:20.590
In 2015 his second daughter, Jasmine was born
to his girlfriend of 9 years, Lauren Hashian.

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:25.350
Dwayne Johnson has risen from humble beginnings
to establish himself as the most bankable

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:27.910
movie star of the 21st century.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:32.170
In the process he has brought back to mainstream
entertainment the sort of alpha male persona

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.560
that has been so absent for so long.

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:59.280
He has become 

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:17.049
the people’s champion once again.

